r raw materials and  when they're fearful that demand is  going to slow down they're gonna be a  lot more hesitant when it comes to  pumping up production initially this was  a disadvantage as companies could not  meet market demand but over time this  has actually become an advantage when  there's a discrepancy between supply and  demand companies can further raise  prices and simply blame it on inflation  and Supply constraints everyone from  milk suppliers to Apple has been doing  this so it's not surprising that chip  companies have jumped onto the trend as  well but all of this brings up the  question how long can this actually last  whether it's next year or three years  from now the supply shortage will  eventually come to an end not to mention  all of the growth factors that we  previously discussed are slowly coming  to an end as well in terms of smartphone  adoption everyone already has a  smartphone Global smartphone sales  literally peaked four years ago and with  the differences between each smartphone  iteration becoming less and less  discernible it's likely that smartphone  sales will not only stagnate but decline  so Chip suppliers like tsmc will have  less and less pricing power over  customers like apple to make things  worse the crypto Community is moving  away from mining as a whole and  switching over to proof of stake  ethereum just wish the proof of stake  just a few weeks ago and that probably  said a president moving forward now none  of this is to say that the chip industry  is going to collapse semiconductors have  become an essential part of modern  society so the industry as a whole is  not going anywhere anytime soon but with  that being said the chip industry is  extremely cyclical and it looks like we  may have just completed the boom phase  at the end of last year this means that  we're probably just at the beginning of  a long and nasty bust phase Nvidia had  one of these phases after the.com boom  and it took Nvidia 15 years to get back  into another boom phase as a customer  this is probably a good thing as demand  levels out and supply issues are  resolved we'll probably see  significantly better value per dollar if  you're an investor however you better  buckle up because regardless of how long  this phase lasts one thing's for sure  and it's gonna be volatile but that's  just what I think do you think  semiconductor margins are too high  comment that down below also drop a like  if you're hoping that the end of this  insanity is near and of course consider  checking out our Discord Community  together ideas and consider subscribing  to see more questions logically answered  but until then I'm Hari and I'll see you  guys on the next one
 

